  "cause": {
    "proximate_text": "hydrogen blower failure due to inadequate stationary blade screw staking. Metallic debris consistent with hydrogen blower blades was found inside the main generator stator core, post failure... Screw staking marks for the missing screw were not made close enough to the screw hole to deform mating surfaces locking the screw in place. With one of three screws detached, the remaining two screws would fail from fatigue resulting in subsequent blower failure.",
    "cause_code": "TBD",
    "category": "provisional",
    "theme": "inadequate screw-staking / blower blade retention leading to stator core damage",
    "provisional": true
  },
